    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "John Cornyn, the forsaken, became the first sitting Republican senator from Texas to lose renomination since 1970, a profound betrayal by the party that severed a long-standing bond. Aided by a late endorsement from the sitting president acting as the meddler, the election candidate's victory reshaped the political landscape.",
